A switch that cannot be flipped is a switch that is not there. The usual cause is an ALWAYS-ASSEMBLED reference to a symbol that only exists under the switch (`X equ y`, a `jp`, a table entry); the fix is an ELSE arm, which costs the shipping build nothing because it is not assembled there.
